{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784525595,"nonce":"WXN5OofNGyOQjym1AeEtf6mY58Q=","message":"The repo Runs screen (`ui/scarab-web-ui/src/routes/RepoView.tsx`) currently only\nhas a status filter (`all` / `running` / `failed`). It should also be filterable\nby:\n\n- **PR number** (`pr_number`)\n- **user / author** (`actor` — the UI labels it \"author\")\n- **branch** (`git_ref`, `refs/{heads,tags}/` prefix stripped)\n\n\nBranch/trigger/PR filters *used* to exist here; they were removed in the\nADR-0054 de-mock (commit `7886ecf`) because the old `RunSummaryDto` didn't carry\nprovenance. That's no longer true: `RunSummaryDto` now stamps `actor`,\n`git_ref`, `pr_number`, `trigger_kind`, and `sha` at creation (ADR-0046/0049).\n`RepoView` already reads them (`refLabel` / `triggerLabel`), so these filters are\n**client-side over the already-fetched rows** — nothing to add on the server,\nunlike the searchable ref picker (which does need `GET .../refs`).\n\nSo this half can ship independently and much sooner. Watch for:\n- Sparse fields — every origin field is independently nullable (e.g. a cron run\n  has no PR, a manual run may have no `actor`); a filter must not hide rows it\n  can't classify unless that filter is actively engaged.\n- Combine with the existing status filter rather than replacing it.\n- Older runs created before origin-stamping carry none of these — treat as\n  \"unmatched\" only when the relevant filter is set.\n\n\nGiven the independence, this is arguably its own PR (client-side, ships now)\nwhile the ref-picker search waits on the new endpoint + a live forge. Keeping\nboth tracked here per request; can split into a sibling ticket if preferred.","files":null}]}